SUMMARY:Deadline: Red Quincho: Beca Constelaciones 2026 (4th Edition)
DESCRIPTION:Beca Constelaciones is Red Quincho's mobility and production gr
 ant for artists\, curators and researchers doing territory-based work\, no
 w in its fourth edition. Each recipient spends one month in residence\, sp
 lit into two 15-day placements at different member spaces across Argentina
 \, pairing an urban and a rural context. The grant covers mobility\, livin
 g costs and production\, with lodging provided. Backed by Fundacion Willia
 ms\, CCEBA and Fundacion Santander through the CABA Mecenazgo scheme. ELIG
 IBILITY IS RESTRICTED: of the 15 grants\, 13 are for people resident in Ar
 gentina and 2 are for people currently living in Spain. Artists\, curators
  and researchers apply through separate forms\; Spanish-based candidates f
 ace an additional jury evaluation. Deadline 9 August 2026 at 23:59 Argenti
 na time.\n\nOrganisation: Red Quincho\nLocation: Rotating urban and rural 
 Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; residency runs September to December
  2026.\nAward: ARS 1\,000\,000 (around USD 690) per grant toward mobility\
 , living costs and production\, plus one month of lodging. 15 grants avail
 able. No application fee.\nDuration: One-month residency split into two 15
 -day placements at different spaces.\n\nMore: https://redquincho.ar/beca-c
 onstelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=refer
 ral
URL:https://redquincho.ar/beca-constelaciones-2026/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rotating urban and rural Red Quincho spaces across Argentina\; res
 idency runs September to December 2026.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-suriname-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260921T042720Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Suriname 2027 (Par
 amaribo\, Moengo\, Frederiksdorp)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or interdisciplinary maker f
 or a three-month residency in 2027 across three locations in Suriname: Par
 amaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\, each with its own cultural\, historic
 al and social context. The residency is inspired by the Surinamese notion 
 of alakondre (literally 'all countries')\, which symbolises living togethe
 r in cultural diversity and emphasises the power of coexisting differences
 . Rather than simply promoting harmony\, alakondre acknowledges historical
  inequalities\, cultural sensitivities and tensions ensuing from colonial 
 and socio-economic realities\, which demands openness and critical awarene
 ss of your position as a creative practitioner\; personal stories\, whethe
 r family history or questions of identity\, can provide powerful entry poi
 nts. A network of local partners supports the residency\, and at each loca
 tion a local maker selected by Surinamese partner organisations works alon
 gside you\, creating natural opportunities for creative exchange and dialo
 gue. ELIGIBILITY: you are an individual designer\, architect or spatial pr
 actitioner\; you are established in the Kingdom of the Netherlands (the Ne
 therlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maar
 ten)\; you are registered in the register of the Dutch Chamber of Commerce
  (KvK) or another business register within the Kingdom of the Netherlands\
 ; and you have run a professional practice within the creative industries 
 for at least four years. NOT open to duos\, collectives or collaborative p
 artnerships\, nor to current recipients of the Talent Development Grant Sc
 heme\, the Open Call Self-taught Designer or the Open Call Emerging Design
  Practices ABCSSS\; accepting this open call means you cannot apply to tho
 se schemes and open calls in 2027. FUNDING: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for the thr
 ee-month residency\; one position is awarded. Assessment takes the form of
  a tender: an external advisory committee ranks proposals on the artistic 
 quality of the work\, the quality of the development plan and the motivati
 on in relation to the residency's objective\, and the highest-scoring prop
 osal is awarded. Decision within eight weeks of the closing date. Submit v
 ia the Creative Industries Fund NL by 21 October 2026\, 16:00 CEST.\n\nOrg
 anisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund
  NL) with local partner organisations in Suriname\nLocation: Residency tak
 es place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\, Moengo and Frederiks
 dorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\
 , Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Kingdom of the Netherla
 nds) and registered in a business register within the Kingdom of the Nethe
 rlands.\nAward: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for a three-month residency\, paid by t
 he Creative Industries Fund NL. One residency position is awarded. No appl
 ication fee.\nDuration: Three months in 2027\, moving between Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/gra
 nts/open-call-residency-suriname?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlan
 ds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Ki
 ngdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
